<title>USA: Ford eyes U.S. and Canada plant closings - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Ford eyes U.S. and Canada plant closings - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford Motor Co, unhappy with poor profitability in its core automotive business, is contemplating plant closings in the U.S. and Canada, The Wall Street Journal reported Thursday.</p>
<p>Though company spokesmen said no decisions have been made, sources say executives have begun to focus on certain likely targets, including the company's factory in Lorain, Ohio, the story said.</p>
<p>It is not likely that any plants would close much sooner than two or three years from now, the story says.</p>
</text>
